Verdict: PASS. It's written to session_plan/eval_task_1.md. The diff removes the hidden token and 10-minute caps on the main agent as the task asked. I did not run the binary: the change only shows up in runs longer than 10 minutes or over 1M tokens, which doesn't fit in this window. My verdict rests on the diff, yoagent's source and the new tests.

• **The fix:** a new function, `main_agent_execution_limits`, now sets the main agent's limits and is called from the build site in the same edit. The turn cap is unchanged (--max-turns, else 200). The token cap is now usize::MAX. The time limit is now set explicitly to Duration::MAX instead of inheriting yoagent's 600s default.
• **No overflow risk:** in yoagent 0.24.2 the two limits are only ever compared against (`context.rs:1206` and `:1213`, both `>=`), and nothing in yoyo does arithmetic on them. So the maximum values can't overflow or panic.
• **Untouched where it should be:** the two other agents capped at one turn (agent_builder.rs:1618 and :1663) are unchanged. Loop detection is kept, and a test checks that.
• **Tests:** the three requested cases are there:
  • the default gives 200 turns, no token cap, and a time limit that differs from yoagent's default;
  • Some(37) changes only the turn cap;
  • the token cap is above the observed stop of 1,061,497.

  They live in a new file, src/agent_limits_tests.rs, because agent_builder.rs is at its size limit; it's registered as a test-only module in src/main.rs.
• **Docs:** there's a CHANGELOG "Unreleased" entry. The `--max-turns` section of `docs/src/configuration/skills.md` now explains the bound, and it also corrects a stale default there (it said 50; the real default is 200). The requested grep over docs/src and README.md finds only that new sentence.

I can't confirm from the diff that the positive control (putting back the 1,000,000 cap and watching the tests fail) was actually run.
